1. Code lineage

  EngTagger began (2009) as a Ruby port of the Perl library
  Lingua::EN::Tagger by Aaron Coburn
  (https://metacpan.org/dist/Lingua-EN-Tagger), which is licensed under
  version 3 of the GNU General Public License.

  Version 2.0 replaces the HMM tagger and probability tables of that
  library with a new averaged-perceptron tagger, tokenizer and trained
  model (lib/engtagger/perceptron.rb, tokenizer.rb, model.rb,
  model_builder.rb), none of which is ported from it. lib/engtagger.rb
  retains routines ported and adapted from Lingua::EN::Tagger for
  extracting nouns, proper nouns and noun phrases, formatting tagged
  output and related text processing, together with its tagset
  conventions. The library keeps the licence of the 0.4 line,
  GPL-3.0-only.

  Lingua::EN::Tagger:
    Copyright 2003-2010 Aaron Coburn
  EngTagger:
    Copyright (c) 2009-2026 Yoichiro Hasebe

  The Porter stemmer (lib/engtagger/porter.rb) is the Ruby implementation
  by Ray Pereda of the Porter stemming algorithm (Martin Porter, 1980),
  from https://tartarus.org/martin/PorterStemmer/, where the
  implementations are offered free of charge for any purpose.

